# Expandable Custom Plan rows and intermediary steps

Replace custom-row tap-to-view navigation with animated inline expansion and ordered construction-step statistics.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Tapping a custom plan main row expands it inline; tapping it again collapses it.
- [x] Holding a custom plan row opens SCR-004-edit directly for that plan.
- [x] Expansion and collapse animate subrows outward smoothly while lower plan rows move in synchrony.
- [x] Each ordered construction action produces one intermediary subrow beneath its plan main row.
- [x] Step subrows appear in exact plan order and use Road, Settlement, or City icons without redundant names.
- [x] A clearly associated fixed-pane label identifies the group as `Steps`.
- [x] Each step row uses the same Mean, Median, 25th, 75th, and turn-probability columns as main rows.
- [x] Fixed labels/icons and scrolling values add/remove matching row heights so alignment is preserved throughout animation and scrolling.
- [x] Cards-only plans with no construction steps omit the Steps section.
- [x] Expansion state remains associated with stable plan identity across player filtering and All-player mode.
- [x] Placeholder intermediary statistics are deterministic and red until simulation milestone output exists.
- [x] Default-plan tap/hold behavior remains unchanged.
- [x] Domain row-model and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused animation/alignment checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This supersedes TASK-013's custom-row tap-to-view behavior. Editing is now the long-press action specified by the updated SCR-002.
- Card-stat subrows are added separately by TASK-030 but share this task's expandable row model and synchronized panes.

## Evidence

- Custom main-row taps now toggle stable UUID-based expansion; long presses open the editor directly.
- A single flattened row collection drives both the fixed pane and both value sections, preserving equal row counts and heights through animated insertion/removal.
- Ordered construction placeholders retain step order, icon-only fixed labels, deterministic player/hand-aware red statistics, and all existing statistical columns.
- Cards-only plans omit the Steps group; default plan interaction is retained.
- Domain tests cover deterministic ordered step rows, and UI edit coverage now exercises direct long-press editing.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing` compiled the app and both test bundles using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks025-030-derived`; live animation checks remain manual.
